# This is an illustrative example of a Tcl-like script to operate the C47/R47.
#
# Commands used here:
#   nim    Numerical entry. Note that you enter as per RPN: negative 4 is
#          entered the RPN way, using the CHS equivalent "-": nim 4 -
#   sin    sin and other standard functions are standard Tcl-like commands.
#   xeq    Executes a loaded user function or a standard function. Below, x!
#          is used as a standard function, as is print x.
#   tsvfn  Changes the TSV output file name: currently 40 char max. .T47.TSV automatically added
#
# This script was called as:
#   ./c47 --headless --script ./res/SCRIPTS/example.t47



nim 1.234
sin
tsvfn Special_Exchange_File
xeq ⎙x

nim 451
xeq x!
xeq ⎙x

nim 0
nim 1.23
nim 66
xeq Xπ
xeq XMULT
nim 0
nim 1.23
nim 66
xeq XDIV

xeq x⇄y
xeq ⎙x




